{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J5zvoxeVxko6XSPw5a8N7F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Stage 03: Implement\n2\t\n3\tInputs: current approved spec for full runs, or combined brief for light runs. A seed-bound run's\n4\tconfirmed `seed-contract.md` and locked checks define it; its `brief.md` may stay the template.\n5\tOutput: `runs/<slug>/03-build/output/plan.md` for full runs, the approved checklist definitions\n6\tin `runs/<slug>/checklist.json` for both profiles, and code in an isolated worktree/clone.\n7\tItems should carry a `check` whenever an automated proof exists; `verify` runs it and no mark is needed.\n8\t\n9\tGate: inspect code and follow the stage 3 gate before implementation; for seed-bound\n10\truns use the guide's [seed definition comparison](../../_system/SDLC.md#seed-definition-comparison).\n11\tFor full runs, write the plan first. Light runs have ONE definition gate, recorded as stage 3 (`sdlc.py decide <run> 3 ...`): the approved `brief.md` + `checklist.json` are the intent, design and plan. An explicit user instruction to execute a reviewed proposal is\n12\timplementation authority; never fabricate separate role approvals.\n13\tEach concurrent writer needs its own checkout. Use the serialized skill wrapper\n14\tin `_system/SDLC.md`; no shared writable skill symlinks or automatic lockfile rewrites.\n15\t\n16\tFor bug fixes, reproduce the expected failure first, obtain independent acceptance,\n17\tand record protected test inputs with `sdlc.py lock-tests`. Implement and verify in\n18\ta loop with stage 04. Update the plan when scope changes and renew stale decisions.\n19\tMark items only with `sdlc.py mark <slug> <item-id> passed|failed --evidence <text>`; never hand-edit receipts.\n20\tFor launcher-managed build agents, use the guide's [pinned build steps](../../_system/SDLC.md#pinned-build-steps).\n21\tRead the supplied step contract, write the handoff at its exact absolute report path,\n22\tand retain that contract and model pin on resume. A missing report refuses step completion.\n23\t\n24\t## Skills\n25\t\n26\tSkillset: `build-skillset` (pin: `.tink/skillsets/build-skillset.json`).\n27\t- Once per machine/library, after reviewing the pin (it selects exact upstream code):\n28\t  `tink library fetch .tink/skillsets/build-skillset.json`\n29\t- At stage open, compile the required disciplines, then start a NEW session so\n30\t  `AGENTS.md` is re-read: `tink use build-skillset --snapshot runs/<slug>/03-build`\n31\t  The launcher does this for you: `python3 _system/scripts/sdlc.py stage <slug> 3`.\n32\t- For a capability gap: `tink-route --receipt runs/<slug>/skills.jsonl \"<what you need>\"`\n33\t  (searches the whole library; prints the skill on stdout. Exit 1 means nothing fits; exit 1 or 2 means\n34\t  continue without a skill).\n35\t\n36\tStage skills (always for this stage; `tink use` compiles the same set):\n37\t- `principle-build-the-lever`: Non-trivial work: build the script or tool that does or proves it, so a reviewer can rerun it, instead of doing it by hand.\n38\t- `unslop`: Any prose you write (docs, commit messages, replies): cut AI tells and filler before you send it.\n39\tWhen one of these applies, read that skill in full before acting on it. In the handoff note, name each skill that changed a decision and the decision it changed.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f309f9c8-1473-4f76-8d79-3d58dcb79201","uuid":"46cf4bd8-7194-494f-b2d9-23d778ae47e2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:49:08.646Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/pi-skimmer/i-delete-pi-skimmer-s-leftover-recovery-folders-myself-from-within-pi-using-a-sk/stages/03-build/CONTEXT.md","content":"# Stage 03: Implement\n\nInputs: current approved spec for full runs, or combined brief for light runs. A seed-bound run's\nconfirmed `seed-contract.md` and locked checks define it; its `brief.md` may stay the template.\nOutput: `runs/<slug>/03-build/output/plan.md` for full runs, the approved checklist definitions\nin `runs/<slug>/checklist.json` for both profiles, and code in an isolated worktree/clone.\nItems should carry a `check` whenever an automated proof exists; `verify` runs it and no mark is needed.\n\nGate: inspect code and follow the stage 3 gate before implementation; for seed-bound\nruns use the guide's [seed definition comparison](../../_system/SDLC.md#seed-definition-comparison).\nFor full runs, write the plan first. Light runs have ONE definition gate, recorded as stage 3 (`sdlc.py decide <run> 3 ...`): the approved `brief.md` + `checklist.json` are the intent, design and plan. An explicit user instruction to execute a reviewed proposal is\nimplementation authority; never fabricate separate role approvals.\nEach concurrent writer needs its own checkout. Use the serialized skill wrapper\nin `_system/SDLC.md`; no shared writable skill symlinks or automatic lockfile rewrites.\n\nFor bug fixes, reproduce the expected failure first, obtain independent acceptance,\nand record protected test inputs with `sdlc.py lock-tests`. Implement and verify in\na loop with stage 04. Update the plan when scope changes and renew stale decisions.\nMark items only with `sdlc.py mark <slug> <item-id> passed|failed --evidence <text>`; never hand-edit receipts.\nFor launcher-managed build agents, use the guide's [pinned build steps](../../_system/SDLC.md#pinned-build-steps).\nRead the supplied step contract, write the handoff at its exact absolute report path,\nand retain that contract and model pin on resume. A missing report refuses step completion.\n\n## Skills\n\nSkillset: `build-skillset` (pin: `.tink/skillsets/build-skillset.json`).\n- Once per machine/library, after reviewing the pin (it selects exact upstream code):\n  `tink library fetch .tink/skillsets/build-skillset.json`\n- At stage open, compile the required disciplines, then start a NEW session so\n  `AGENTS.md` is re-read: `tink use build-skillset --snapshot runs/<slug>/03-build`\n  The launcher does this for you: `python3 _system/scripts/sdlc.py stage <slug> 3`.\n- For a capability gap: `tink-route --receipt runs/<slug>/skills.jsonl \"<what you need>\"`\n  (searches the whole library; prints the skill on stdout. Exit 1 means nothing fits; exit 1 or 2 means\n  continue without a skill).\n\nStage skills (always for this stage; `tink use` compiles the same set):\n- `principle-build-the-lever`: Non-trivial work: build the script or tool that does or proves it, so a reviewer can rerun it, instead of doing it by hand.\n- `unslop`: Any prose you write (docs, commit messages, replies): cut AI tells and filler before you send it.\nWhen one of these applies, read that skill in full before acting on it. In the handoff note, name each skill that changed a decision and the decision it changed.\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01J5zvoxeVxko6XSPw5a8N7F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
