{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LL6x823FeSquREp3M4egiL","type":"tool_result","content":"308\t`launch` and `resume` recheck every definition gate and perform offline exact-model\n309\tresolution before admitting a provider-capable adapter operation. Both receive the\n310\tstored pin and absolute report path regardless of caller cwd or changed defaults. The\n311\tagent prompt must identify the run's approved input files: `runs/<run>/brief.md` for\n312\tlight runs, or `runs/<run>/01-plan/output/intent.md`, `02-design/output/spec.md` and\n313\t`03-build/output/plan.md` for full runs, plus `stages/03-build/CONTEXT.md`. It names the\n314\texact report destination and prohibits running `sdlc.py step`, `stage` or `decide`. The\n315\tadapter marks the child environment with\n316\t`TINK_SDLC_STEP_SESSION=1`; while set, `sdlc.py step` refuses `prepare`, `launch`,\n317\t`resume` and `complete` (read-only `show` remains available), preventing recursive\n318\tstep admission independently of prompt compliance.\n319\tResume also carries the same session identity; it must not silently start another\n320\tsession. The adapter owns delivering the contract/report instructions to the agent.\n321\t`complete` requires an active step, a nonempty regular report at the exact\n322\trecorded path and the adapter's offline confirmation that the agent finished its\n323\tlatest turn on the pin, then stores the report digest. A paused, stopped, failed or\n324\tstill-running agent leaves the step `active`: resume it, then complete. Missing reports refuse completion: no root\n325\tfallback, copying or invented report. A report is not proof of passing checks,\n326\tauthenticated authorship, approval, or release; existing `verify` and forge gates\n327\tremain independent. API 1 status and capabilities are unchanged.\n328\t\n329\t### Trusted launcher adapter contract\n330\t\n331\tArbitrary Pi/Herdr commands are not compatible. A launcher is reviewed executable code\n332\timplementing `tink-sdlc-launcher` protocol 1 (one is bundled for Pi, below):\n333\t\n334\t- Offline probe: `ADAPTER resolve --for-operation launch|resume --model PIN\n335\t  --report ABS --contract ABS` (plus `--session ID` for resume). It must make **zero\n336\t  provider requests**, check the exact model is available/compatible and validate\n337\t  the retained session's model before resume. Never resolve an alias or fall back.\n338\t- Admission: `ADAPTER launch|resume --model PIN --report ABS --contract ABS`\n339\t  (plus `--session ID` for resume). It must pass the pin explicitly to the harness\n340\t  and recheck it before any provider request, not rely on mutable defaults. It\n341\t  returns after session admission, not after the whole build; no shell is used.\n342\t- Finished probe: `ADAPTER finished --model PIN --report ABS --contract ABS --session ID`.\n343\t  It must make **zero provider requests** and reply `finished: true` only when the\n344\t  retained session's newest turn ended normally on the pin. `complete` refuses on\n345\t  `false`, a failure or a missing probe.\n346\t- Each operation returns exit zero and one JSON object on stdout containing\n347\t  `protocol: \"tink-sdlc-launcher\"`, integer `api_version: 1`, `operation` (launch, resume"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f309f9c8-1473-4f76-8d79-3d58dcb79201","uuid":"70a05824-63ed-4d88-ba18-90d2041339d0","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:49:19.908Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jondev/dev/worktrees/pi-skimmer/i-delete-pi-skimmer-s-leftover-recovery-folders-myself-from-within-pi-using-a-sk/_system/SDLC.md","content":"`launch` and `resume` recheck every definition gate and perform offline exact-model\nresolution before admitting a provider-capable adapter operation. Both receive the\nstored pin and absolute report path regardless of caller cwd or changed defaults. The\nagent prompt must identify the run's approved input files: `runs/<run>/brief.md` for\nlight runs, or `runs/<run>/01-plan/output/intent.md`, `02-design/output/spec.md` and\n`03-build/output/plan.md` for full runs, plus `stages/03-build/CONTEXT.md`. It names the\nexact report destination and prohibits running `sdlc.py step`, `stage` or `decide`. The\nadapter marks the child environment with\n`TINK_SDLC_STEP_SESSION=1`; while set, `sdlc.py step` refuses `prepare`, `launch`,\n`resume` and `complete` (read-only `show` remains available), preventing recursive\nstep admission independently of prompt compliance.\nResume also carries the same session identity; it must not silently start another\nsession. The adapter owns delivering the contract/report instructions to the agent.\n`complete` requires an active step, a nonempty regular report at the exact\nrecorded path and the adapter's offline confirmation that the agent finished its\nlatest turn on the pin, then stores the report digest. A paused, stopped, failed or\nstill-running agent leaves the step `active`: resume it, then complete. Missing reports refuse completion: no root\nfallback, copying or invented report. A report is not proof of passing checks,\nauthenticated authorship, approval, or release; existing `verify` and forge gates\nremain independent. API 1 status and capabilities are unchanged.\n\n### Trusted launcher adapter contract\n\nArbitrary Pi/Herdr commands are not compatible. A launcher is reviewed executable code\nimplementing `tink-sdlc-launcher` protocol 1 (one is bundled for Pi, below):\n\n- Offline probe: `ADAPTER resolve --for-operation launch|resume --model PIN\n  --report ABS --contract ABS` (plus `--session ID` for resume). It must make **zero\n  provider requests**, check the exact model is available/compatible and validate\n  the retained session's model before resume. Never resolve an alias or fall back.\n- Admission: `ADAPTER launch|resume --model PIN --report ABS --contract ABS`\n  (plus `--session ID` for resume). It must pass the pin explicitly to the harness\n  and recheck it before any provider request, not rely on mutable defaults. It\n  returns after session admission, not after the whole build; no shell is used.\n- Finished probe: `ADAPTER finished --model PIN --report ABS --contract ABS --session ID`.\n  It must make **zero provider requests** and reply `finished: true` only when the\n  retained session's newest turn ended normally on the pin. `complete` refuses on\n  `false`, a failure or a missing probe.\n- Each operation returns exit zero and one JSON object on stdout containing\n  `protocol: \"tink-sdlc-launcher\"`, integer `api_version: 1`, `operation` (launch, resume","numLines":40,"startLine":308,"totalLines":637}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LL6x823FeSquREp3M4egiL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
